# Production defaults shared across all three regional Vercel projects.
# Region-specific values (currency, tax rate, DB replica, callback URLs) live
# in .env.production.kenya / .env.production.ethiopia / .env.production.somalia.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file intentionally contains NO real secrets. Actual values
# for STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, MPESA_CONSUMER_SECRET, DATABASE_URL, etc. are set
# per-project in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings -> Environment
# Variables) or via `vercel env add <NAME> production`, scoped to each
# region's Vercel project. See vercel.json and README for the deployment
# pipeline (git push -> Vercel auto-deploy).

NODE_ENV="production"

# Database: unified write model — all regions write to the primary
# (Kenya / AWS RDS eu-west-2, London). Each region's Vercel project sets
# DATABASE_URL to this primary and DATABASE_REPLICA_URL to its own
# regional read replica (af-south-1 for Ethiopia, eu-west-2 for Somalia).
# Both are injected as Vercel secrets, not stored in this file.
DATABASE_URL=""
DATABASE_REPLICA_URL=""

# Stripe operates across all regions with one production account.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""
BETTER_AUTH_URL=""
